  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This attractive laceleaf comes from Pennsylvania. The medium-sized, finely cut leaves emerge orange-red and change to a pleasant medium green for the summer, then turn golden-yellow in the fall. A second flush of leaves in midsummer is coppery red, gradually turning green. 'Chantilly Lace' is hardy and fairly vigorous, forming a mushroom-shaped mound up to 8 ft. (2.5 m) tall."
  },
